  "scope": "Two fresh, single-control-plane Kind Kubernetes v1.36.1 clusters compare the same seven measured API operations under broad and selective audit policies. The policy comparison checks finite event selection, retained write detail, and a reduction in sampled poll bytes. A third isolated cluster checks five TLS webhook event deliveries, one transient 503 retry, and native audit counters. A fourth isolated cluster makes two 400-KiB synthetic ConfigMap writes to observe the 1-MiB file-rotation threshold and exact-once retention in active and rotated files. These finite fixtures do not model sustained traffic, production capacity, retention adequacy, alert delivery, I/O pressure, real AI traffic, or cluster-wide coverage.",
